1
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:13,800
(Let it go.)

2
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:45,980
=Revenge From A Wife=

3
00:00:46,540 --> 00:00:48,200
=Episode 2=

4
00:00:50,820 --> 00:00:52,260
Grass gives it form.

5
00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:54,300
Simplicity conceals mastery.

6
00:00:57,420 --> 00:00:59,029
(Xiao Che, the Emperor)

7
00:00:59,071 --> 00:01:00,690
Roujia would've loved it.

8
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:05,050
My sister always loved

9
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:06,820
simple things like this.

10
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:08,620
I'm sure her spirit is moved

11
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:10,770
by Your Majesty's devotion.

12
00:01:11,490 --> 00:01:13,260
Which artisan made this?

13
00:01:14,740 --> 00:01:16,620
I want to reward him in person.

14
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:18,330
Your Majesty,

15
00:01:19,130 --> 00:01:20,410
fate was unkind to him.

16
00:01:20,770 --> 00:01:22,050
After finishing this screen,

17
00:01:22,380 --> 00:01:23,570
he had an accident

18
00:01:23,770 --> 00:01:24,620
and passed away.

19
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:29,570
An accident?

20
00:01:31,330 --> 00:01:32,290
Rushing it for the memorial

21
00:01:32,490 --> 00:01:33,740
must've taken its toll.

22
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:36,100
He was too frail to endure it.

23
00:01:36,490 --> 00:01:37,719
I've already had his body

24
00:01:37,761 --> 00:01:39,490
sent back to his hometown.

25
00:01:39,930 --> 00:01:41,210
His family will be compensated.

26
00:01:48,410 --> 00:01:49,410
What a pity.

27
00:01:51,260 --> 00:01:53,050
Such craftsmanship is rare.

28
00:01:53,570 --> 00:01:54,850
Roujia had a kind heart.

29
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:58,020
She couldn't bear to see people suffer.

30
00:01:59,930 --> 00:02:01,020
Ask the Imperial Household Department

31
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:03,330
to grant his family more aid

32
00:02:04,020 --> 00:02:04,930
as a testament to

33
00:02:05,410 --> 00:02:06,850
Roujia's compassion.

34
00:02:09,490 --> 00:02:10,210
Your Majesty,

35
00:02:10,900 --> 00:02:12,850
he's only a grass weaver.

36
00:02:16,290 --> 00:02:17,130
Yes.

37
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:19,410
I understand.

38
00:02:42,010 --> 00:02:43,290
Don't be afraid, Shouhe.

39
00:02:44,570 --> 00:02:45,780
I'm here.

40
00:02:47,060 --> 00:02:48,340
I'll see you off.

41
00:03:42,290 --> 00:03:43,500
(My wife,)

42
00:03:44,060 --> 00:03:44,850
(Wanniang,)

43
00:03:46,820 --> 00:03:47,980
(I must)

44
00:03:48,450 --> 00:03:49,890
(go on ahead.)

45
00:03:52,820 --> 00:03:54,130
(Don't seek revenge.)

46
00:03:55,980 --> 00:03:57,610
(Let this matter rest.)

47
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:00,940
Let go.

48
00:05:04,410 --> 00:05:05,460
(Shouhe,)

49
00:05:07,410 --> 00:05:09,170
(let me stay with you a little longer.)

50
00:05:56,610 --> 00:05:57,220
Wanniang.

51
00:05:58,290 --> 00:05:58,930
What's wrong?

52
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:00,660
Where's my benefactor?

53
00:06:01,050 --> 00:06:01,810
Shouhe...

54
00:06:02,610 --> 00:06:03,460
He's dead.

55
00:06:06,930 --> 00:06:07,490
Mother.

56
00:06:07,810 --> 00:06:09,140
You were His Majesty's wet nurse.

57
00:06:09,340 --> 00:06:10,340
You must know what to do.

58
00:06:12,490 --> 00:06:14,020
My husband only went to the palace

59
00:06:14,660 --> 00:06:15,930
(Qing'er, Nanny Liu's Daughter)
to earn enough

60
00:06:16,700 --> 00:06:18,100
for a fur collar for me.

61
00:06:19,020 --> 00:06:20,660
But when he came home,

62
00:06:21,730 --> 00:06:23,580
only half his body remained.

63
00:06:24,250 --> 00:06:25,250
(Nanny Liu, the Emperor's Wet Nurse)
His clothes

64
00:06:25,370 --> 00:06:26,900
were stuffed with dry grass.

65
00:06:30,610 --> 00:06:32,810
Consort Chen took my husband from me

66
00:06:34,250 --> 00:06:36,540
and made me lose our child too.

67
00:06:37,610 --> 00:06:38,460
Nanny Liu,

68
00:06:39,340 --> 00:06:40,220
can you really let go

69
00:06:40,700 --> 00:06:42,460
of what happened back then?

70
00:06:42,850 --> 00:06:44,460
I lie here day after day.

71
00:06:45,220 --> 00:06:46,730
How could I let it go?

72
00:06:55,930 --> 00:06:56,850
Back then,

73
00:06:57,290 --> 00:07:00,250
I only lit one incense stick in secret
for the late Empress.

74
00:07:01,050 --> 00:07:02,660
Consort Chen had my leg sawed off

75
00:07:03,850 --> 00:07:05,460
and drove me out of the palace.

76
00:07:06,140 --> 00:07:08,540
I wish I could tear her apart.

77
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:10,410
But in this condition,

78
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:12,780
I can't even make it out the door.

79
00:07:13,810 --> 00:07:15,290
Then let me go back in your place.

80
00:07:16,140 --> 00:07:17,370
I'll make Consort Chen

81
00:07:17,610 --> 00:07:18,850
pay in blood for what she did.

82
00:07:21,610 --> 00:07:23,050
I can get you into the palace.

83
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:24,780
But...

84
00:07:25,780 --> 00:07:27,540
First, you have to die once.

85
00:07:33,290 --> 00:07:35,170
I've already died once.

86
00:07:51,970 --> 00:07:54,980
♪Sunset fades beyond the lonely city♪

87
00:07:56,350 --> 00:07:59,180
♪Dusk snow paints the green hills♪

88
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:02,420
♪A lone rider storms the old pass♪

89
00:08:02,740 --> 00:08:04,490
♪Drunk, I gaze by lamplight♪

90
00:08:04,950 --> 00:08:08,390
♪Old friends have all drifted away♪

91
00:08:09,220 --> 00:08:12,380
♪My broken sword rusts, as do I♪

92
00:08:13,590 --> 00:08:16,740
♪Jackdaws cry into the night♪

93
00:08:17,660 --> 00:08:19,999
♪Half a banner snaps in the wind♪

94
00:08:20,041 --> 00:08:22,170
♪In dreams, I return to the camps♪

95
00:08:22,350 --> 00:08:25,420
♪Moonlight chills my armor♪

96
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:29,570
♪Life is a dream through many winters♪

97
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:34,620
♪I gaze beyond the edge of the world♪

98
00:08:35,210 --> 00:08:37,450
♪Parting sorrow spills across the moon♪

99
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:41,800
♪The moon and wind mean nothing now♪

100
00:08:43,260 --> 00:08:46,399
♪History turns to ash before ink dries♪

101
00:08:46,441 --> 00:08:51,620
♪Who plays the zither
and sighs at the pavilion?♪

102
00:08:52,970 --> 00:08:59,900
♪The past has faded away♪

103
00:08:59,900 --> 00:09:03,900
♪The past has faded away♪
